WEBVTT

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.980
Royal capital, here I am!

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.930
And so, I've finally made it 
to the capital, Onii-chan!

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.200
You're opening a shop here?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.420
Yep! Straight to a realtor I go 
to secure a suitable property!

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.920
The referral letter from 
Count Bozes really helped!

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.270
I see. But don't you need furnishings?

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.830
I hired a local craftsman 
to renovate the place.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.800
Oh, but there's a bunch of stuff 
I brought over from Earth via jumping.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.830
Makes sense.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.190
You've gotten one step closer to 
fulfilling your ambitions, sister of mine!

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.700
<i>Yes, for a happy retirement...</i>

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.850
Hello there. 
I've just moved in next door.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.070
<b>Small Gift</b>

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.070
<b>General Store Mitsuha</b>

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.070
Here's a towel for you. 
Please use it if you'd like.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.130
Oh, you shouldn't have...

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.760
It's so soft!

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.530
We have more for sale!

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.620
<i>I'm going to save up 80,000 gold!</i>

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.180
Hello!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.210
Ah, here!

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:25.950
Take one!

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.890
What is this, paper?

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.210
It's so thin and smooth!

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.710
<i>General Store Mitsuha's 
officially open for business!</i>

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:38.220
General Store Mitsuha

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.890
Mm-hmm, looking good!

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.930
Mostly stocked from 100-yen shops!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.700
A rotating selection of somewhat 
luxury items and convenience goods.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.440
I chose things that you'd be sad to see 
go away, but aren't strict necessities.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.080
<i>These are for myself.</i>

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.820
All righty, then!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.370
Now all that's left is to wait 
for some customers!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.780
Well, it's only the first day...

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.300
This isn't like a supermarket 
grand opening sale! That's right!

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.970
No, it's only the second day...

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.360
Why? Why can't I get any customers?!

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.540
<i>Should I keep the shop open until later?</i>

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.860
<i>But that means I have to 
work longer hours...</i>

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.970
<i>What to do? What to do?!</i>

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.120
<i>Finally!</i>

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.240
Welcome!

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.850
Ah, er... this shop just opened, right?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.570
Yes! We just started two days ago!

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.870
Please take your time browsing!

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.850
<i>That was a close one...</i>

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.050
<i>I'll just drive them away 
if I'm too aggressive.</i>

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.230
<i>Let's wait and watch.</i>

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.250
What's this?

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.940
That's a fish scaler.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:18.290
You can easily remove fish scales with it, 
so it's very handy for cooking.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.040
C-Cooking fish?!

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.630
Remove fish scales?

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.530
<i>Hmm? Is something weird?</i>

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.560
That's a high-brightness flashlight.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.160
A useful pole that extends and retracts.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.380
Superglue to stick things 
together in a flash!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.010
<i>It didn't work! They don't seem 
like they'll buy anything!</i>

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.390
Hair cleanse elixir?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.370
Yes!

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:51.890
It's a magic elixir that cleans your hair 
and hydrates damaged hair!

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.990
Soap does exist in this world, 
and it's used to wash hair.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.440
But it's expensive, runs out quickly, 
and isn't cost-effective or high-quality.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:06.010
In contrast, this two-in-one shampoo...

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.650
can be used dozens of times with one bottle!

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:13.240
A bargain item that keeps your hair 
beautifully glossy and smooth!

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.460
Did you say dozens of times?!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.410
Glossy...

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.530
Smooth...

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.200
Yes! I'd stake this store's reputation on it!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.170
Eight silver...

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.800
Hmm, that's asking a bit too much...

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.690
No way!

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:26.870
Yep...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.310
<i>I mean, I know eight silver is no small 
amount for a commoner to spend,</i>

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.540
<i>but you'd know if you tried it! If only...</i>

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.450
Please wait!

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.620
Would one of you like to try 
a complimentary sample?

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.020
Huh? For free?

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.720
Hmm, but I'm pretty hungry now.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.080
We agreed to go and get 
some good food today!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:49.740
Yeah!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.940
<i>Ah! I'd finally gotten customers!</i>

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.990
<i>My very first customers!</i>

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.410
<i>It might be the end for me if I let them go!</i>

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:00.000
<i>They mustn't leave! They mustn't leave!</i>

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.040
<i>They mustn't...</i>

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.830
I-I know!

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.580
I'll get you some good food! So please!

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.300
Huh? I thought this was a general store.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.430
It's a special promotion 
for our grand opening!

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.660
For free! On the house!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.730
I can guarantee its taste!

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.090
It'll be better than any 
restaurant in the city!

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.360
So please try a sample!

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.240
Sure. We'll leave it to you, then.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.200
Thank you so much...

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.700
Wh-What's this?!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.630
A thin jet of... hot water is coming out!

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.110
A magic wand from which 
hot water springs forth...

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:42.780
Hey, are you all right, Anke?!

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.680
Yeah. It feels pretty good!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.570
<i>Okay, now get a good taste of this!</i>

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:58.120
<i>The power of magic hair cleanse elixir, 
that is, two-in-one shampoo!</i>

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:02.150
Huh?

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.040
<i>It... it's not lathering up at all!</i>

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:15.530
<i>There we go!</i>

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:23.130
I'm sorry. Usually you only need one pump, 
but I ended up using three.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.470
It seems there was 
an awful lot of dirt there...

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:27.490
Am I... dirty?

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:29.080
Ah, I'm so sorry!

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.090
<i>I treated a customer like she was filthy...</i>

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.120
As an apology, I'll add 
on a sample of body wash...

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.100
I mean, body cleanse elixir!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.520
Wow! This feels really good, as well!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.210
It smells nice...

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.440
Costs just eight silver!

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.330
What's this? It's so warm!

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.780
A magic mallet that creates hot wind...

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.490
Wow! This is so amazing!

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.490
H-Her hair really is glossy and smooth!

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.290
That magic elixir really is magic!

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.630
I want the hair cleanse elixir for sure...

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.100
But I want the body cleanse elixir, as well!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.070
Me, too!

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:07.610
They're eight silver each... 
So 16 silver for both?

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.360
But I only have 12 silver on me...

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.420
I have nine silver...

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.590
I've got 10 silver.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.530
Then why don't you each contribute eight silver,

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:18.630
purchase one bottle each of hair 
cleanse and body cleanse elixir,

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.570
and share them among the three of you?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.980
Huh? Isn't that eight silver too many?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.570
All of these are eight silver apiece!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.120
It looks great on you.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:32.900
I'll take it!

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.160
Thank you very much for your purchase!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.850
Shall we eat now, then?

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:48.400
Wh-What's that?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.090
There's a fire without any firewood...

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:56.550
Cooking
for Witches

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.280
Magic elixirs, magic wands, 
mallets, and a magic oven...

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.550
A witch?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.000
Hey! Don't say weird things like that!

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.680
Thanks for waiting!

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.770
First up is minestrone... Ah, some soup.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:08.540
Huh? Y-You just started cooking!

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.150
Is this fully cooked?

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.180
Of course!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.540
D-Delicious!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.490
It's got a strong flavor with depth to it!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.880
Frankly, it's way better 
than the meals back at the manor!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.420
Mm-hmm!

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.470
What's in this?

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.630
<i>Okay, they liked it!</i>

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.840
<b>Delicious, full of veggies
Minestrone
A robust soup slowly simmered with care
 1 portion (150g)</b>

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.330
<i>Okay, next up is buri daikon.</i>

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.790
<i>Also in a retort pouch.</i>

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.530
<i>Flavor absorbed into every bite!</i>

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.020
This is a dish made using fish.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:45.860
What?!

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.550
F-Fish?

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:50.170
Hmm? What's wrong with fish?

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.020
N-No, it's nothing!

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.430
Really, it's nothing!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:59.250
<i>Huh? What's with their reaction to fish?</i>

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.720
<i>Is it taboo or something? Did I screw up?</i>

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:06.590
<i>No, they're eating it just fine.</i>

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:08.040
<i>Well, whatever.</i>

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.630
<i>Let's keep going! Next!</i>

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.840
This is a risotto made with grains.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.380
Am I just imagining things, or...

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:21.080
are all of these dishes 
coming from the same pot?

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.650
Ah, don't say that!

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.720
I was trying to ignore it!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.140
I-I'm sure it's fine... probably!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.600
<b>Buri
Daikon</b>

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.930
This is roast beef.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.680
<i>What in the world?!</i>

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.300
This is beef simmered in soy sauce.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.770
<i>I-I don't believe it!</i>

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.490
This is beef stew.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.240
<i>Sho good... It's all so good!</i>

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.490
And ice cream for your dessert.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.960
I've never had anything like this!

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:53.040
And finally, some amazake as a warm drink.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.390
Did you enjoy your meal?

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.700
Y-Yeah!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:03.000
All of it was something new 
I'd never tried before, and...

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.340
That pot—

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.510
All of it was delicious!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.480
Thank you so much!

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.720
<i>It worked out...</i>

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.020
If you'd like, please accept this as 
a souvenir to share with your colleagues.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.740
Oh, make sure to take 
the wrapper off before you eat them.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.320
Thank you very much!

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.090
<i>I did it!</i>

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:32.070
<i>My first sale to my first customers!</i>

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:35.600
<i>I splurged quite a bit, 
but still plenty of profit!</i>

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:41.120
If those three spread the word, 
I might see a rush of new customers!

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.870
Ah, but then things might get too hectic!

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.930
I won't have time for bathroom breaks!

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:48.000
What will I do?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.230
What should we do?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:06.310
We should do as she said, 
and share them with our colleagues!

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:08.150
Eh, then...

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:12.290
I-In all the stories, things never end well 
when you don't do as you're told!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.580
We'll give them to the head chef, Marcel!

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.960
Marcel!

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.230
Here.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:25.180
What's this? Some kind of food?

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:29.440
A witc—stranger gave them 
to us as a souvenir.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:32.570
She said to take the wrapper off 
before you eat one!

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:33.620
What?

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:42.650
It's got a vaguely sweet, rich aroma...

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.380
M-Marcel?! Are you ok—

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.160
Delicious!

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.200
Satisfyingly crunchy!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.870
A toasty flavor!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.920
Indescribably sweet!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.170
And its depth!

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.370
What the heck is this?!

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.970
Hey! Just where'd you get your hands on...

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:03.970
You there.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.430
What's all the commotion?

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.230
M-My lady.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.930
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.980
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.690
And so she gave you these.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.700
Y-Yes...

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:25.200
What do you make of this, my dear?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.570
Hmm. A witch, you say...

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.790
I'm sure she's a friendly witch!

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.250
A magic elixir...

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.850
Let me use some of this.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:38.560
Huh?

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:41.630
If it's money, I can pay a measly 16 silver!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.390
I'll return it to you 
after I've tried it once.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:46.880
Please, help yourself.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.090
Very well.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:50.760
Furthermore, Britta...

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.300
that brooch of yours...

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:53.670
Ah, yes.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.030
We also bought this for eight silver.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.010
What?!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:59.940
How could such a splendid 
brooch cost just eight silver?!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:04.380
You see, these aren't real 
gemstones as you might think,

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.480
and in fact happen to be man-made...

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.800
You're saying these are imitations?!

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.950
Making them with magic 
requires zero investment...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:15.140
That aside, is it true you were 
served a dish made using fish?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:18.270
Not dried, smoked, or salted?

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:19.210
Yes.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.770
As a child, I tried fish once 
at a seaside village.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:25.050
There's no mistaking it.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:27.720
All the other dishes 
were just so scrumptious, as well!

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.220
Quite frankly, it sounds preposterous.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:35.040
It's 10 days by wagon from a seaside 
fishing village to the royal capital.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.350
A stagecoach would still take seven days.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:42.630
Even a bespoke carriage running nonstop 
day and night, swapping horses and drivers,

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.270
would still take three days.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.390
Besides, if you transported them that way,

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:49.360
a single fish would fetch 
more than a small gold coin.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:55.280
And that's still only possible in the 
winter, making use of snow and ice.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.750
It's simply impossible at this time of year.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.200
It wouldn't work even if you stewed 
the fish and reheated it periodically.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.880
Not only would it take too much time,

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.940
it'd be unfit to be served 
after simmering for so long.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:11.050
It seems no amount of pondering 
will lead us to a solution.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:16.990
However, my lord, if we can get our hands 
on novel ingredients or cooking methods...

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.730
Yes. Perhaps she might be of assistance.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.190
Look into it, Marcel.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:24.400
Yes. Please leave it to me.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.110
Welcome!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.920
Please feel free to take a basket.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.030
Hm? Sure...

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.700
<i>Okay! I've just opened, 
and already a customer!</i>

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.660
<i>Things are starting to look up!</i>

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.770
<i>He's looking at the fish scaler, as well.</i>

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.710
<i>Is there something there after all?</i>

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.050
<i>This is...</i>

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.760
<i>Oh! He's taken notice of the knife!</i>

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.380
<i>I put that there to say,</i>

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.840
<i>"This shop has high-end 
products in stock, too!</i>

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:58.470
<i>Behold the technical prowess on display!"</i>

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.670
<i>Wait, you're buying it?!</i>

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:05.060
<i>What a shocker. 
Guess its quality shines through.</i>

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.020
Thank you for your purchase!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.930
<i>Mostly cooking related, huh?</i>

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.030
<i>I bet this person's a chef.</i>

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.640
Excuse me, but could you confirm 
the price before I buy these?

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.460
Yes, of course!

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:21.090
That "fish scaler", was it?

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.340
Why are you selling something like that?

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.540
Huh? It's just a handy item.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:30.170
I thought I could sell them to housewives 
who are good at cooking fish...

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.410
Come now!

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:36.130
There's no way you can get your hands on 
fresh fish that need scaling in this town!

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.970
Do you know just how far 
we are from the sea?!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:39.760
Ah!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:43.240
<i>That's right! No wonder 
everyone reacted that way!</i>

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:46.440
<i>Oh, no! I stocked the wrong item!</i>

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.880
Also, if you could tell me how to use these.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.240
Oh, sure.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.810
This is a peeler.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:54.400
Even a complete novice can use this

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.690
to perfectly peel vegetables 
at veteran speeds.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:00.400
An underhanded tool 
to undermine expert chefs.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.240
Wha?!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.390
This is an hourglass.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:07.100
The sand falls below and always 
runs out in the same span of time.

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:10.170
It's a handy tool for precisely 
measuring boiling times and the like.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:12.510
This is a can opener.

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:16.430
You use it to open cans that preserve 
foods as-is for years on end...

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.950
Are you all right?

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.220
Y-Yes...

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.820
Then please tell me one more thing.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.130
Why is this so expensive?

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:25.960
Hmph!

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:32.230
That's because this is no mere plaything, 
made by pouring iron into a mold!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.650
Forged from carefully chosen steel, 
the finest of all materials,

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.840
by an artisan who's devoted 
decades to crafting knives!

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:43.610
Created by a veritable ogre of steel, 
it's practical, yet also a work of art!

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.210
A supreme blade!

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.080
A-An ogre of steel?!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.350
Take a closer look.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:50.110
Folded over and over at high temperatures,

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.550
hard steel and soft steel hammered 
together with forge welding!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.220
With both a sharp edge and strong durability,

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.930
a miraculous work of the gods!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:03.180
To be honest, even if I sell this, 
I make zero profit.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:06.220
No profit? Then, why?!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.150
Seeing that the finest products 
are delivered from artisan to chef...

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.150
that is a merchant's calling.

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:17.570
Any cheaper, and artisans 
can't make a living...

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.320
Any pricier, and chefs can't afford them...

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:27.080
In that case, I don't see a problem 
with incurring a slight expense myself.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.000
I...

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.740
I'll take it!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:31.290
You're too kind!

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.680
By the way, missy, if I could 
have a word with the manager...

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.640
Ah, sure thing.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:43.930
Please feel free to ask anything.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.020
Huh?

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:49.540
I bought this store, renovated it, 
and stock its goods.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.630
In other words, I'm the owner and manager.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.690
Eh?

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.270
Then, let me ask you.

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:01.700
Is it possible to buy 
fresh fish at this store?

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:05.580
<i>So that's his real business with me?</i>

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.910
Where'd you hear that?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.010
From Anke and the others.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.000
Who's that?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.160
I believe there were three 
girls who visited yesterday.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.500
Ah!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.250
<i>Those three really did 
spread the word! Thank you!</i>

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:24.470
They were our first customers, 
so I really overdid it with the freebies.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:26.100
I'm really in the red now!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.810
So why fish?

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:34.630
From what you said, it seems the people 
in this town don't eat fish very often.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:38.780
My name is Marcel.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.900
I serve as the chef for 
the house of Viscount Reiner.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:46.520
The previous head chef fell ill, 
so I was suddenly asked to take over.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:50.580
For some time, I managed 
to smoothly run the kitchen...

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:53.220
Was there some sort of problem?

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:53.920
Yes.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.990
It concerns the catering 
for Miss Adelaide's debutante ball.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:02.260
Debutante ball?

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:06.890
Aristocratic women make their debut 
into society when they turn 15.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:11.640
It's a party to celebrate this coming of age 
and serve as an unveiling.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:15.570
You could even say a debutante ball

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:19.030
decides one's place 
and future in high society.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:23.490
Fumble it, and you'll be met with snide 
remarks and talking behind your back.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:29.320
Which is why noble houses spare no expense 
in matters such as the catering and dress.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.730
What would amount to 
a fortune for a commoner...

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.930
ends up being spent for a single night.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.790
Whoa!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:40.160
Viscount Reiner's family is new 
aristocracy in its second generation,

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:43.420
and they're not regarded highly 
by other nobles as is...

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:48.680
We cannot allow failure 
or incompetence at the debutante ball!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.940
Yet I lack confidence.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.450
I have little experience 
with parties at such a scale.

00:20:56.450 --> 00:21:01.610
And up against chefs serving major 
noble houses and the royal palace...

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:07.580
I fear I'll embarrass my lord 
and his daughter.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:11.400
Ashamed as I am, it scares me so.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:18.290
So you wanted to astound everyone 
with a dish made with fish?

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.780
Hmm...

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:26.430
<i>Should I just sell him 
some fish and call it quits?</i>

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:31.640
<i>I'd make money and help him out, 
which is a win all around...</i>

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.100
<i>But what is this feeling I'm getting?</i>

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:38.600
<i>This sounds like a fun project!</i>

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:44.510
In fact, we happen to run a broad service 
for dealing with such problems.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:48.890
From relationship advice 
to land administration,

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.990
General Store Mitsuha 
is available for consultation!

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:53.950
Fees subject to negotiation!
